-- Welcome post for the 2026 Executive Leadership administration. Source photo
-- is a designed flyer graphic (headshot grid + chapter crest/100th-anniversary
-- mark + name/title overlays), so photo_fit is 'contain' to keep the whole
-- graphic visible rather than cropping it to a 4:5 frame.
insert into public.news_highlights
  (slug, brother_name, label, title, preview, body, photo_url, photo_fit, published, published_at)
values
  (
    'sigma-lambda-2026-executive-leadership',
    'Sigma Lambda Chapter',
    'ANNOUNCEMENT',
    'A New Year of Service, Leadership, and Excellence: Sigma Lambda Chapter Welcomes Its 2026 Executive Leadership',
    'As a new fraternal year begins, the Sigma Lambda Chapter proudly welcomes its 2026 executive leadership administration, led by Bro. Dr. Brian L. Turner, President, and Bro. Rev. Dr. Patrick C. Thompson, Vice President.',
    E'As a new fraternal year begins, the Sigma Lambda Chapter of Alpha Phi Alpha Fraternity, Inc. proudly welcomes its 2026 leadership administration, a team prepared to build upon the chapter''s legacy of service, brotherhood, scholarship, and excellence.\n\nUnder the leadership of Bro. Dr. Brian L. Turner, President, and Bro. Rev. Dr. Patrick C. Thompson, Vice President, the 2026 executive committee stands ready to serve the brothers of Sigma Lambda and continue advancing the chapter''s mission in the Greater New Orleans community.\n\nThe administration brings together brothers serving across the chapter''s executive and operational leadership, including:\n• Bro. Dr. Brian L. Turner — President\n• Bro. Rev. Dr. Patrick C. Thompson — Vice President\n• Bro. Gilbert Jones — Treasurer\n• Bro. Wayne Woods, Esq. — Parliamentarian\n• Bro. Malik Bartholomew — Historian\n• Bro. Jarred Jupiter — Corresponding Secretary\n• Bro. Kendrick Miller — Chaplain\n• Bro. Robert Mitchell, Jr. — Director of Education\n• Bro. Howard Rodgers, IV — Dean of Membership\n• Bro. Dexter Joseph — Sergeant at Arms\n• Bro. Kael Saloy — Recording Secretary\n• Bro. Dr. Marc Barnes — Associate Editor to The Sphinx\n• Bro. Ralph Johnson — Member at Large\n• Bro. Robert Carter, III — Member at Large\n• Bro. Terrol Perkins — Member at Large\n\nTogether, this executive committee represents a collective commitment to ensuring that Sigma Lambda remains a chapter where brotherhood is strengthened, leadership is developed, and service remains at the center of the work.\n\nContinuing a Century of Excellence\n\nThe new administration assumes its responsibilities during a particularly meaningful period for Sigma Lambda. With the chapter carrying the distinction of 100 years of Alpha excellence in New Orleans, the work of today''s brothers is connected to a century-long legacy established by those who came before them.\n\nLeadership in Alpha Phi Alpha is more than holding a title. It is a responsibility to the Brotherhood, to the community, and to the ideals upon which the Fraternity was founded.\n\nAs Sigma Lambda moves into another year, the administration will have the opportunity to build upon the accomplishments of previous leaders while creating new opportunities for education, community engagement, mentorship, fellowship, and service.\n\nThe charge is clear: serve with purpose, lead with integrity, and leave the chapter stronger for those who follow.\n\nA Prayer for the Work Ahead\n\nAs these brothers begin their respective terms of service, Sigma Lambda looks not only to their experience and leadership, but also to divine guidance for the journey ahead:\n\n"May God guide our thoughts and control our lives so that we may become through Thee servants of all."\n\nThat spirit provides an appropriate foundation for the year ahead. Leadership is ultimately about service—to the Brotherhood, to the community, and to a purpose greater than oneself.\n\nThe 2026 administration now steps forward with a shared responsibility: to serve, to lead, and to continue the legacy.\n\nOne Brotherhood. One Legacy. One Future.\nService. Leadership. Excellence.\n\nThe Sigma Lambda Chapter congratulates and welcomes its 2026 executive leadership and looks forward to a year of continued achievement, meaningful service, and Alpha excellence.',
    '/images/news/26leadership-team.jpg',
    'contain',
    true,
    '2026-09-22 12:00:00+00'
  )
on conflict (slug) do nothing;
